rs to forward ReadIndex messages with equal rctx to the leader before any quorum acknowledgment, then deliver the quorum ack and eight further heartbeat rounds with acks from both followers; count read index answers per requester while confirming the leader stays in StateLeader. Controls: the identical shape with distinct rctxes (both requesters must be answered) and a single requester retrying its own rctx (that requester must be answered), which separate a duplicate-rctx admission loss from a broken harness or a generally stalled leader.\",\n      \"disposition\": \"active\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"add_request\",\n        \"advance\",\n        \"leader_msg_read_index\",\n        \"heartbeat_resp_completion\",\n        \"response_to_req\",\n        \"send_read_index_response\",\n        \"node_read_index_contract\",\n        \"rawnode_read_index_api\",\n        \"test_frees_read_only_mem\",\n        \"test_readindex_to_old_leader\"\n      ],\n      \"counterevidence\": [\n        \"node.go:218-229 states that callers must not reuse an rctx and that the reuse restriction is only lifted starting with release-3.7, so the silent drop may be the documented behaviour of this release-3.6 revision rather than an implementation error; this draft reports the mechanism and the observed starvation, and leaves that classification to human review.\",\n        \"The same-requester retry case is answered: when one requester retries its own rctx while the status is pending, the single response is addressed to that requester, so the observed starvation requires a requester whose equal-rctx message is discarded because another requester was admitted first.\",\n        \"Existing test coverage (raft_test.go:1192-1222) exercises one unique rctx and only checks that the queue and pending map drain; node_test.go:196-241 forwards two equal rctxes from different nodes but asserts only that the messages are forwarded and never checks for read index answers.\"\n      ],\n      \"limitations\": [\n        \"Only ReadOnlySafe is exercised; ReadOnlyLeaseBased and the pendingReadIndexMessages path (a leader that has not yet committed an entry in its term) are out of scope for this experiment.\",\n        \"The observation window is eight leader heartbeat rounds with quorum acknowledgments in one process; it establishes repeated nonprogress under normal opportunities rather than an unbounded guarantee.\",\n        \"The requester-side application contract (matching ReadStates by RequestCtx) is read from node.go / rawnode.go rather than executed.\"\n      ],\n      \"resume_conditions\": [],\n      \"knowledge\": [],\n      \"open_gaps\": [],\n      \"latest_execution\": {\n        \"id\": \"5827db69173840a595c972e79565bcde\",\n        \"experiment_id\": \"708eebc14c4040feb495e11d064001d0-experiment\",\n        \"status\": \"completed\",\n        \"exit_code\": 0,\n        \"record\": \"logs/5827db69173840a595c972e79565bcde/check.json\",\n        \"observations\": \"logs/5827db69173840a595c972e79565bcde/observations.json\"\n      },\n      \"latest_interpretation\": null,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"investigations\",\n        \"id\": \"708eebc14c4040feb495e11d064001d0-question-0\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"knowledge\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"708eebc14c4040feb495e11d064001d0-knowledge-0\",\n      \"revision\": 1,\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"statement\": \"In StateLeader with the ReadOnlySafe option, when a MsgReadIndex arrives whose Entries[0].Data equals the rctx of a request that is already recorded in readOnly.pendingReadIndex, readOnly.addRequest returns early without storing the new request message, and sendMsgReadIndexResponse still attaches a heartbeat with that rctx (bcastHeartbeatWithCtx) and re-acknowledges the local node; the readIndexQueue and pendingReadIndex therefore keep exactly one status for the two admissions, and no second request message is retained.\",\n      \"conditions\": \"Node is in StateLeader, ReadOnlyOption is ReadOnlySafe (the default), the leader has committed an entry in its current term so stepLeader calls sendMsgReadIndexResponse directly, the earlier request with the equal rctx is still pending (not yet advanced), and no reset/become* has occurred between the two admissions.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"add_request\",\n        \"send_read_index_response\",\n        \"leader_msg_read_index\"\n      ],\n      \"executions\": {},\n      \"operation_id\": \"708eebc14c4040feb495e11d064001d0\",\n      \"uses\": [],\n      \"last_correction\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"708eebc14c4040feb495e11d064001d0-knowledge-1\",\n      \"revision\": 1,\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"statement\": \"On the acknowledging heartbeat, stepLeader asks readOnly.advance for the statuses up to the acknowledged ctx and then answers each returned status through responseToReadIndexReq(rs.req, rs.index): a status whose stored request came from a remote peer produces one MsgReadIndexResp addressed to that stored request's From, and a status whose stored request came from the leader itself appends one local ReadState. Only the request message of the first admission with a given rctx is stored, so admissions that were discarded by addRequest produce no read index answer of either kind.\",\n      \"conditions\": \"ReadOnlySafe with a quorum of heartbeat acknowledgments carrying the ctx, leader state unchanged between admission and acknowledgment, and the discarded admission having used the same rctx bytes as the stored one.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"heartbeat_resp_completion\",\n        \"response_to_req\",\n        \"advance\"\n      ],\n      \"executions\": {},\n      \"operation_id\": \"708eebc14c4040feb495e11d064001d0\",\n      \"uses\": [],\n      \"last_correction\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"experiments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"708eebc14c4040feb495e11d064001d0-experiment\",\n      \"investigation_id\": \"708eebc14c4040feb495e11d064001d0-question-0\",\n      \"previous_id\": null,\n      \"basis\": \"fixed-experiments/708eebc14c4040feb495e11d064001d0-experiment/basis.json\",\n      \"results\": [\n        {\n          \"prerequisites\": null,\n          \"parsing_errors\": [],\n          \"experiment_id\": \"708eebc14c4040feb495e11d064001d0-experiment\",\n          \"check_id\": \"5827db69173840a595c972e79565bcde\",\n          \"outcome\": \"violated\",\n          \"confirmed\": false,\n          \"reviewed_complete\": false,\n          \"blockers\": [\n            \"Exploratory basis has no fixed requirement and comparison\",\n            \"Execution has no attributed interpretation\"\n          ],\n          \"gap_ids\": [],\n          \"interpretation_id\": null\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"reselection\": {\n    \"task\": [\n      \"A1: CFT decision formation and progress.\",\n      \"A2: Context and authority acquisition, transition and loss.\"\n    ],\n    \"target\": {\n      \"repo\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/etcd-raft\",\n      \"snapshot_id\": \"a23faff7cd3e43b9af4254953ad0f9e7\"\n    },\n    \"directed_question\": null,\n    \"questions\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"708eebc14c4040feb495e11d064001d0-question-0\",\n        \"question\": \"On a stable leader using ReadOnlySafe, can a ReadIndex request that carries an rctx equal to one that is still pending complete, or is that request silently discarded so that its requester receives no read index answer while the cluster kee\",\n        \"disposition\": \"active\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"add_request\",\n          \"advance\",\n          \"leader_msg_read_index\",\n          \"heartbeat_resp_completion\"\n        ],\n        \"open_gap_count\": 0,\n        \"latest_interpretation\": null\n      }\n    ],\n    \"recent_knowledge\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"708eebc14c4040feb495e11d064001d0-knowledge-0\",\n        \"revision\": 1,\n      